@Vitalita.API_HostAddress = http://localhost:5240

### OpenAPI document (Spanish)
GET {{Vitalita.API_HostAddress}}/swagger/v1/swagger.json
Accept: application/json
Accept-Language: es

### Unknown route: 404 ProblemDetails with "message", localized in Spanish
GET {{Vitalita.API_HostAddress}}/api/v1/does-not-exist
Accept: application/json
Accept-Language: es
Origin: http://localhost:5173

### Same request in English (default culture)
GET {{Vitalita.API_HostAddress}}/api/v1/does-not-exist
Accept: application/json

### CORS preflight from the Vite dev server
OPTIONS {{Vitalita.API_HostAddress}}/api/v1/does-not-exist
Origin: http://localhost:5173
Access-Control-Request-Method: PUT
Access-Control-Request-Headers: authorization,content-type

### IAM: sign up (Caregiver by default). 201 + Location; 409 if the email exists; 400 if role=Admin
POST {{Vitalita.API_HostAddress}}/api/v1/authentication/sign-up
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: es

{
  "email": "andrea.mendoza@vitalita.pe",
  "password": "Vitalita123",
  "role": "Caregiver"
}

### IAM: sign up as Admin is rejected with 400
POST {{Vitalita.API_HostAddress}}/api/v1/authentication/sign-up
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "not.an.admin@vitalita.pe",
  "password": "Vitalita123",
  "role": "Admin"
}

### IAM: sign in. 200 with id, email, role, status and token; 401 for wrong credentials or inactive account
# @name signIn
POST {{Vitalita.API_HostAddress}}/api/v1/authentication/sign-in
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "andrea.mendoza@vitalita.pe",
  "password": "Vitalita123"
}

### IAM: public email lookup. Array with zero or one {id, email}
GET {{Vitalita.API_HostAddress}}/api/v1/users?email=andrea.mendoza@vitalita.pe
Accept: application/json

### IAM: get a user by id (Bearer token; own user or Admin)
GET {{Vitalita.API_HostAddress}}/api/v1/users/{{signIn.response.body.id}}
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{signIn.response.body.token}}
